<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3350] Don&apos;t allow set cronExecutionUser</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3350</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3045&quot; title=&quot;Add the option which prevents the cron executing user from being changed to users other than the login user&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-3045&quot;&gt;ZEPPELIN-3045&lt;/a&gt; also try to fix the issue, but seems no update for a long time. This is a critical security issue for zeppelin. The cron module may need to revisit to redesign and improve, but as a quick fix, I think we can just don&apos;t allow set cronExecutionUser, and just run the note via the note owner.  \cc &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=moon&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;moon&quot;&gt;moon&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=felixcheung&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;felixcheung&quot;&gt;felixcheung&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=prabhjyotsingh%40apache.com&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;prabhjyotsingh@apache.com&quot;&gt;prabhjyotsingh@apache.com&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jongyoul&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jongyoul&quot;&gt;jongyoul&lt;/a&gt; thoughts ?&lt;/p&gt;
